0..71 Comment "// Loops and their exits. A `loop` or a `while` may run forever, so the"
72..143 Comment "// function holding one states `Div` in its row, `-F [Div] T`: the host"
144..221 Comment "// interface with no operation, which nothing handles (#1481). A caller holds"
222..298 Comment "// it in its own row, and an entry runs at `+U (-F [Div] T)`. A `for` over a"
299..373 Comment "// list descends on the list and needs no entry; each `become` is an exit."
